From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SushyDev <mail@sushy.dev>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 23:08:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: don't apply the wide bus divisor to the link rate
 check

msm_dp_bridge_mode_valid() halves the pixel clock when wide bus is
available and then uses that halved value both for the
DP_MAX_PIXEL_CLK_KHZ limit and for the link bandwidth comparison.

Wide bus carries two pixels per pixel clock between the DPU and the DP
controller.  That halves the rate the controller has to be clocked at,
which is what DP_MAX_PIXEL_CLK_KHZ bounds, but it does not change how
much data the link has to carry.  Using the halved clock understates the
requirement by a factor of two, so modes that cannot fit are reported
MODE_OK and go black when selected.

On a Samsung Odyssey G85SB, 2560x1440@175 needs 17.9 Gbps and was
offered on a link providing 17.28 Gbps.

YUV 4:2:0 genuinely halves the transferred data, so it keeps the divisor
for the bandwidth calculation; only the wide bus term is dropped.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index dc31572..46a5ce1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -700,6 +700,7 @@ enum drm_mode_status msm_dp_bridge_mode_valid(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	struct msm_dp *dp;
 	int mode_pclk_khz = mode->clock;
 	int mode_pclk_orig = mode->clock;
+	int link_pclk_khz = mode->clock;
 
 	dp = to_dp_bridge(bridge)->msm_dp_display;
 
@@ -716,6 +717,10 @@ enum drm_mode_status msm_dp_bridge_mode_valid(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	     msm_dp_wide_bus_available(dp))
 		mode_pclk_khz /= 2;
 
+	if (drm_mode_is_420_only(&dp->connector->display_info, mode) &&
+	    msm_dp_display->panel->vsc_sdp_supported)
+		link_pclk_khz /= 2;
+
 	if (mode_pclk_khz > DP_MAX_PIXEL_CLK_KHZ)
 		return MODE_CLOCK_HIGH;
 
@@ -728,9 +733,9 @@ enum drm_mode_status msm_dp_bridge_mode_valid(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 		mode_bpp = 8;
 	else
 		mode_bpp = msm_dp_panel_get_mode_bpp(msm_dp_display->panel,
-					mode_bpp, mode_pclk_khz);
+					mode_bpp, link_pclk_khz);
 
-	mode_rate_khz = mode_pclk_khz * mode_bpp;
+	mode_rate_khz = link_pclk_khz * mode_bpp;
 	supported_rate_khz = link_info->num_lanes * link_info->rate * 8;
 
 	if (mode_rate_khz > supported_rate_khz)
